From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:22:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] xmllite: end a document where it ends.

A document that ended with elements still open had its last node read
again on every call, an element one level deeper each time, so a caller
reading to the end never got there. Answer MX_E_INPUTEND there, as
Windows does, and keep answering it. Text the document ends in is the
whole node, and a comment, section or instruction it ends in, or a name
it cuts off, is the error Windows gives for each.

The markup that ends a comment, section or instruction could lie across
two of the chunks read from the stream, and then was not seen at all.
While the declaration was read, reading more converted again what had
been converted already: a UTF-16 document got the start twice, and a
UTF-8 one that was nothing but its declaration failed an assertion.

A document without a root element, or with a second one, is
WC_E_ROOTELEMENT; an XML declaration anywhere but at the start is
WC_E_TEXTXMLDECL; and a document with no byte order mark and no '<' to
tell its encoding by is UTF-8, however short.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8b58e3c5b347ad9967f0564fb3f925c55d7c7149)

